cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "h-delta: online learning from verified work on one consumer GPU"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "MaxGR"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A testbed for a language model (Qwen2.5-3B) that learns online from tool-verified work.
  A bolt-on fast-weight slice is compared with a reason cache, small learners and online LoRA
  on identical held-out items; LoRA with replay dominates. Also measures a confidence gate and
  reason-keyed failure memory. Carried out mostly by an AI coding agent under the author's
  direction.
keywords:
  - continual learning
  - fast weights
  - LoRA
  - test-time learning
  - agent memory
